  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:4665",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to interact with Ephrin type-A receptor 3 through a shared pathway involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which acts as a target of multiple entities. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C targets Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, NCI-H1734, or Tyrosine-protein kinase Fer, all of which are targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol. This indicates a potential mechanism where Ent-Gloeosteretriol serves as a bridge, facilitating the interaction between Oblonganoside C and Ephrin type-A receptor 3. The consistent involvement of Ent-Gloeosteretriol in linking Oblonganoside C to Ephrin type-A receptor 3 suggests a possible regulatory or signaling role, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where Ent-Gloeosteretriol mediates the effect of Oblonganoside C on Ephrin type-A receptor 3, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism.",
